2026-09-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2256) 'WebTransport inside a sandbox guest
 # uuid: 607ebf0a-c6e3-504c-bd91-8321aec5349c
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2256) 'A godot-sandbox guest carries bulk game traffic over QUIC, HTTP/3 and WebTransport at binary-translated speed, and the first channel it carries mints tokens from a key the host never sees
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2256) 'a godot-sandbox guest ELF running the QUIC stack, the zone server and clients that host it, and a token-minting channel; `interactor-fabric-zone`'s ELFs (RFD66606-2287) are its first user
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2256) 'A sandbox guest carries QUIC traffic and mints tokens from a key the host never sees.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2256) 'A key on the desk, or a helper that hands out a token, is open to every script there.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2256) 'The signer's app key stays in guest memory. Each token request is checked against a tuple.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2256) 'a token-minting guest over WebTransport
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2256) 'QUIC, HTTP/3 and WebTransport run inside a RISC-V guest ELF that libriscv binary-translates to near native speed: picoquic with h3zero, TLS 1.3 through picotls on mbedTLS. The first channel is a signer on a zone server whose app key lives only in guest memory. It checks a ReBAC tuple and returns a one-hour installation token, never the key.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2256) '- RFD66606-2255 (SSH tunnel to Bao), the path the signer peer's identity can use to reach Bao.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2256) '- RFD66606-2060 (org-scoped app token), the token this mints.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2256) '- RFD66606-2200 (ReBAC agent roles as tuples), the authorization.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2256) 'The host's part
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2256) 'The host relays UDP through `PacketPeerUDP` and ticks timers without seeing plaintext.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2256) 'The exchange
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2256) '1. The signer guest starts, logs in to Bao with its own cert identity over mTLS terminated inside the guest, and reads the app key into guest memory.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2256) '2. An agent's guest opens a WebTransport session to the zone server on UDP 7443 and sends a mint request naming itself.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2256) '3. The signer checks `agent:<cn>#mint@app:<app>` in the relationship store and refuses without it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2256) '4. It signs a JWT, exchanges it for an installation token over TLS inside the guest, and returns the token and its expiry.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2256) 'What is not settled
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Throughput.** Bulk game traffic needs the binary-translated guest to keep up with a native QUIC stack. Nothing is measured yet; the comparison is the same stack built native against the translated guest, same payload, same link.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Per-call instruction budget.** Translation shortens a TLS 1.3 handshake but does not remove the sandbox's per-call limit, so the budget for this guest is set from a measured handshake.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Transport.** WebTransport is the proposal; ENet through the existing ENet sandbox is the fallback if the translated QUIC guest cannot carry the traffic.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Licences.** picoquic, picotls and mbedTLS are MIT or Apache-2.0. libriscv and godot-sandbox are BSD-3-Clause, so an MIT-or-Apache-only rule needs an exception for the host.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2256) '- **Which peer.** A zone server the operator runs, on owned hardware or the existing hosting; the choice decides who can read that peer's memory.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2256) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2256) 'Only a separate peer keeps it out of reach.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2256  1 LINE
 Text:Written

